{"id":"mahabharata-7-011","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":11,"title":"एकादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 11 · Drona promises to seize Yudhishthira","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya tells how Drona, on becoming commander, said he would capture Yudhishthira alive but not kill him, and Duryodhana proclaimed the plan through the army. Drona's wish was to secure Duryodhana's cause only if Arjuna were kept away.","kn":"ಸೇನಾಪತಿಯಾದ ದ್ರೋಣ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲದೆ ಜೀವಂತ ಹಿಡಿಯುವೆನೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿದ್ದನ್ನೂ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಇದನ್ನು ಸೈನ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಾರಿದ್ದನ್ನೂ ಸಂಜಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನನ್ನು ದೂರ ಒಯ್ದರೆ ಮಾತ್ರ ಇದು ಸಾಧ್ಯವೆಂದು ದ್ರೋಣ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"संजय बताते हैं कि सेनापति बनकर द्रोण ने युधिष्ठिर को मारे बिना जीवित पकड़ने की बात कही और दुर्योधन ने सेना में इसकी घोषणा की। द्रोण ने कहा कि यह तभी सम्भव है जब अर्जुन को दूर रखा जाए।","te":"సేనాపతి అయిన ద్రోణుడు యుధిష్ఠిరుని చంపకుండా సజీవంగా పట్టుకుంటానన్నాడని, దుర్యోధనుడు సేనలో ప్రకటించాడని సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు. అర్జునుని దూరంగా తీసుకెళితేనే ఇది సాధ్యమని ద్రోణుడు అంటాడు.","ta":"படைத்தலைவரான த்ரோணர் யுதிஷ்டிரரைக் கொல்லாமல் உயிருடன் பிடிப்பதாகக் கூறியதையும், துரியோதனன் அதைப் படையில் அறிவித்ததையும் சஞ்சயன் சொல்கிறான். அர்ஜுனன் விலகினால்தான் இது இயலும் என்று த்ரோணர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"ദ്രോണർ സേനാനായകനായപ്പോൾ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ ജീവനോടെ പിടികൂടുമെന്നും കൊല്ലില്ലെന്നും പറഞ്ഞത് സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനൻ ആ പദ്ധതി സേനയിൽ പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു. അർജുനനെ അകറ്റിനിർത്തിയാൽ മാത്രമേ ദുര്യോധനന്റെ കാര്യം സുരക്ഷിതമാക്കൂ എന്നതായിരുന്നു ദ്രോണരുടെ ആഗ്രഹം."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.11; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"द्रोणाभिषेकपर्व","titleEn":"Dronabhisheka Parva (Drona's consecration)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"हन्त ते वर्णयिष्यामि सर्वं प्रत्यक्षदर्शिवान् ।\nयथा स न्यपतद्द्रोणः सादितः पाण्डुसृञ्जयैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Very well, I will describe to you everything as an eyewitness, how Drona fell, brought down by the Pandavas and Srinjayas."}},{"n":2,"text":"सेनापतित्वं संप्राप्य भारद्वाजो महारथः ।\nमध्ये सर्वस्य सैन्यस्य पुत्रं ते वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having received the command, the great chariot-warrior, Bharadvaja's son, spoke to your son in the middle of the whole army."}},{"n":3,"text":"यत्कौरवाणामृषभादापगेयादनन्तरम् ।\nसेनापत्येन मां राजन्नद्य सत्कृतवानसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Since today, O king, you have honored me with the command next after the bull of the Kauravas, the son of Apaga,"}},{"n":4,"text":"सदृशं कर्मणस्तस्य फलं प्राप्नुहि पार्थिव ।\nकरोमि कामं कं तेऽद्य प्रवृणीष्व यमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"receive, O king, a fruit fitting for that deed. What wish of yours shall I fulfill today? Choose whatever you wish.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनश्चिन्त्य कर्णदुःशासनादिभिः ।\nतमथोवाच दुर्धर्षमाचार्यं जयतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana, after consulting Karna, Duhshasana and others, said to that unassailable teacher, best of the victorious:"}},{"n":6,"text":"ददासि चेद्वरं मह्यं जीवग्राहं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nगृहीत्वा रथिनां श्रेष्ठं मत्समीपमिहानय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you give me a boon, then seize Yudhishthira alive, the best of chariot-warriors, and bring him here to me.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः कुरूणामाचार्यः श्रुत्वा पुत्रस्य ते वचः ।\nसेनां प्रहर्षयन्सर्वामिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the teacher of the Kurus, hearing your son's words, gladdening the whole army, said these words."}},{"n":8,"text":"धन्यः कुन्तीसुतो राजा यस्य ग्रहणमिच्छसि ।\nन वधार्थं सुदुर्धर्ष वरमद्य प्रयाचसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Fortunate is Kunti's son, the king, whom you wish to seize. You ask today, unassailable one, for a boon that is not for his killing."}},{"n":9,"text":"किमर्थं च नरव्याघ्र न वधं तस्य काङ्क्षसि ।\nनाशंससि क्रियामेतां मत्तो दुर्योधन ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why, tiger among men, do you not want his death? Surely, Duryodhana, you do not hope for this deed from me."}},{"n":10,"text":"आहोस्विद्धर्मपुत्रस्य द्वेष्टा तस्य न विद्यते ।\nयदिच्छसि त्वं जीवन्तं कुलं रक्षसि चात्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or perhaps the son of Dharma has no enemy, since you want him alive and are protecting your own family."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ वा भरतश्रेष्ठ निर्जित्य युधि पाण्डवान् ।\nराज्यांशं प्रतिदत्त्वा च सौभ्रात्रं कर्तुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or, best of the Bharatas, do you wish, after defeating the Pandavas in battle, to give them back a share of the kingdom and make peace with them?"}},{"n":12,"text":"धन्यः कुन्तीसुतो राजा सुजाता चास्य धीमतः ।\nअजातशत्रुता सत्या तस्य यत्स्निह्यते भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fortunate is Kunti's son the king, and well born is that wise man. His being without enemies is true, since you are fond of him.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"द्रोणेन त्वेवमुक्तस्य तव पुत्रस्य भारत ।\nसहसा निःसृतो भावो योऽस्य नित्यं प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Drona spoke thus to your son, O Bharata, the feeling that ever worked in him suddenly came out."}},{"n":14,"text":"नाकारो गूहितुं शक्यो बृहस्पतिसमैरपि ।\nतस्मात्तव सुतो राजन्प्रहृष्टो वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even those equal to Brihaspati cannot hide a change of expression. So your son, O king, delighted, said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"वधे कुन्तीसुतस्याजौ नाचार्य विजयो मम ।\nहते युधिष्ठिरे पार्थो हन्यात्सर्वान्हि नो ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Teacher, in killing Kunti's son in the battle there is no victory for me. If Yudhishthira is killed, Partha will surely kill all of us."}},{"n":16,"text":"न च शक्यो रणे सर्वैर्निहन्तुममरैरपि ।\nय एव चैषां शेषः स्यात्स एवास्मान्न शेषयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And even all the immortals could not kill them all in battle. And whoever of them remained would not leave us."}},{"n":17,"text":"सत्यप्रतिज्ञे त्वानीते पुनर्द्यूतेन निर्जिते ।\nपुनर्यास्यन्त्यरण्याय कौन्तेयास्तमनुव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if Yudhishthira of true vow is brought, and defeated again at dice, the sons of Kunti and those who follow him will go again to the forest."}},{"n":18,"text":"सोऽयं मम जयो व्यक्तं दीर्घकालं भविष्यति ।\nअतो न वधमिच्छामि धर्मराजस्य कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So my victory will plainly last a long time. For that reason I never wish the death of the king of Dharma.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्य जिह्ममभिप्रायं ज्ञात्वा द्रोणोऽर्थतत्त्ववित् ।\nतं वरं सान्तरं तस्मै ददौ संचिन्त्य बुद्धिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing his crooked intention, Drona, who knew the truth of things, wise, thought it over and gave him that boon with a condition."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"न चेद्युधिष्ठिरं वीर पालयेदर्जुनो युधि ।\nमन्यस्व पाण्डवं ज्येष्ठमानीतं वशमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If Arjuna does not protect Yudhishthira in battle, hero, consider the eldest Pandava as brought under your control."}},{"n":21,"text":"न हि पार्थो रणे शक्यः सेन्द्रैर्देवासुरैरपि ।\nप्रत्युद्यातुमतस्तात नैतदामर्षयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Partha cannot be faced in battle even by gods and asuras with Indra. So, dear one, I do not accept this."}},{"n":22,"text":"असंशयं स शिष्यो मे मत्पूर्वश्चास्त्रकर्मणि ।\nतरुणः कीर्तियुक्तश्च एकायनगतश्च सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is without doubt my pupil, and he excelled me in the use of weapons. Young, renowned and devoted to one goal,"}},{"n":23,"text":"अस्त्राणीन्द्राच्च रुद्राच्च भूयांसि समवाप्तवान् ।\nअमर्षितश्च ते राजंस्तेन नामर्षयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"he has obtained many weapons from Indra and from Rudra. And he is angry with you, so I do not tolerate him."}},{"n":24,"text":"स चापक्रम्यतां युद्धाद्येनोपायेन शक्यते ।\nअपनीते ततः पार्थे धर्मराजो जितस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let him be drawn away from the battle by whatever means is possible. When Partha is removed, the king of Dharma is defeated by you."}},{"n":25,"text":"ग्रहणं चेज्जयं तस्य मन्यसे पुरुषर्षभ ।\nएतेन चाभ्युपायेन ध्रुवं ग्रहणमेष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you regard his capture as victory, best of men, then by this means capture will surely come."}},{"n":26,"text":"अहं गृहीत्वा राजानं सत्यधर्मपरायणम् ।\nआनयिष्यामि ते राजन्वशमद्य न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having seized the king, devoted to truth and dharma, I will bring him under your control today, O king, without doubt,"}},{"n":27,"text":"यदि स्थास्यति संग्रामे मुहूर्तमपि मेऽग्रतः ।\nअपनीते नरव्याघ्रे कुन्तीपुत्रे धनंजये ॥","meaning":{"en":"if he stands before me in battle even for a moment, with the tiger among men Dhananjaya, Kunti's son, drawn away."}},{"n":28,"text":"फल्गुनस्य समक्षं तु न हि पार्थो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nग्रहीतुं समरे शक्यः सेन्द्रैरपि सुरासुरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But in the presence of Phalguna, Partha Yudhishthira cannot be seized in battle even by gods and asuras with Indra.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":29,"text":"सान्तरं तु प्रतिज्ञाते राज्ञो द्रोणेन निग्रहे ।\nगृहीतं तममन्यन्त तव पुत्राः सुबालिशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Drona had vowed the king's capture with a condition, your very foolish sons thought he was already caught."}},{"n":30,"text":"पाण्डवेषु हि सापेक्षं द्रोणं जानाति ते सुतः ।\nततः प्रतिज्ञास्थैर्यार्थं स मन्त्रो बहुलीकृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son knew that Drona was partial toward the Pandavas, so to make the promise firm he spread that counsel widely."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनेनापि ग्रहणं पाण्डवस्य तत् ।\nसैन्यस्थानेषु सर्वेषु व्याघोषितमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana too, destroyer of foes, proclaimed the capture of the Pandava in all the army camps."}}]}]}